      "writtenOn": "2017-08-21T08:41:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need to climb the sched domain hierarchy to account for cluster-level energy. That way the scheduler is aware that waking up a CPU in an idle cluster is expensive (probably more than in a busy cluster, although this might depend on OPP alterations and the actual energy model)",
